ter' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>11.34</td></tr><tr style='background-color: #FFFFFF;'><th align='center' style='background-color: #D3D3D3; font-weight: bold; border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>4</th><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>0.71</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>1.06</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>1.92</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>3.36</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>5.39</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>7.78</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>9.49</td><td align='center' style='border: 1px solid gray; padding: 5px;'>13.28</td></tr></table><br/><table style="border: 1px solid black; border-collapse: collapse; "><colgroup width="160"></colgroup> <colgroup width="80"></colgroup> <colgroup width="80"></colgroup> <colgroup width="100"></colgroup> <colgroup width="80"></colgroup> <tr><th align='center' style='background-color: lightgray'>Phenotype</th> <th align='center' style='background-color: lightgray'>Expected</th> <th align='center' style='background-color: lightgray'>Observed</th> <th align='center' style='background-color: lightgray'>Calculation</th> <th align='center' style='background-color: lightgray'>Statistic</th> </tr><tr><td>&nbsp;Yellow Round (Y&ndash;R&ndash;)</td> <td align='center'>90</td> <td align='center'>86</td> <td align='center'><sup>(86-90)&sup2;</sup>&frasl;&nbsp;<sub>90</sub></td> <td align='center'>0.178</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;Yellow Wrinkled (Y&ndash;rr)</td> <td align='center'>30</td> <td align='center'>22</td> <td align='center'><sup>(22-30)&sup2;</sup>&frasl;&nbsp;<sub>30</sub></td> <td align='center'>2.133</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;Green Round (yyR&ndash;)</td> <td align='center'>30</td> <td align='center'>35</td> <td align='center'><sup>(35-30)&sup2;</sup>&frasl;&nbsp;<sub>30</sub></td> <td align='center'>0.833</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;Green Wrinkled (yyrr)</td> <td align='center'>10</td> <td align='center'>17</td> <td align='center'><sup>(17-10)&sup2;</sup>&frasl;&nbsp;<sub>10</sub></td> <td align='center'>4.900</td></tr><tr><td colspan='4' align='right' style='background-color: lightgray'>(sum) &chi;&sup2;&nbsp;=&nbsp;</td> <td align='center'>8.044</td></tr></table><br/><p>The final result gives the chi-squared (&chi;&sup2;) test value of 8.04 with 2 degrees of freedom. Consulting the Table of &chi;&sup2; Critical Values and a level of significance &alpha;=0.05, we obtain a critical value of 5.99.</p><p>Since the chi-squared value of 8.04 is greater than the critical value of 5.99, the null hypothesis has BEEN REJECTED.</p><hr/> <p>Your lab partner completed a chi-squared (&chi;&sup2;) test on your lab data (above) for the F<sub>2</sub> generation in a standard dihybrid cross. The goal was to verify if the observed results matched the expected phenotype ratios.</p><p>However, it appears they made an error. <strong>What did they do wrong?</strong></p>
PROMPT_F660_D9E5
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_1';
The numbers in the calculation have to be squared and they are not squared.
LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_2';
The wrong rejection criteria was used. the significance level, &alpha; is wrong.
LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_3';
The degrees of freedom is wrong, it should be a different value.
LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_4';
The expected progeny for the null hypothesis is incorrect. They did the calculation wrong.
LITERAL_F660_D9E5_CHOICE_4
